# Only consulted for builds whose context is the repo root — currently just the Feature 068
# webapp images (apps/webapp/backend/Dockerfile, apps/webapp/frontend/Dockerfile). The other
# apps build from their own subdirectory as context, so this file does not affect them.
.git
**/.venv
**/venv
**/node_modules
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
**/dist
**/.pytest_cache
**/htmlcov
**/.mypy_cache

# Runtime data / logs — never belong in an image (the webapp reads data via a read-only mount).
apps/denidin-app/dev_data
apps/denidin-app/data
apps/denidin-app/test_data
apps/*/logs
apps/*/test_data
apps/*/dev_data
**/*.log
shared
artifacts

# Not COPYed by either webapp Dockerfile — keep them out of the (repo-root) build context so
# the context transfer to the daemon stays small. Backend COPYs only apps/webapp/backend/ +
# apps/denidin-app/src/ + apps/morning-mcp-app/src/ (+ a few named files); frontend only apps/webapp/frontend/.
# morning-mcp-app: only src/ is COPYed (backend Dockerfile - Clients tab imports MorningClient).
apps/morning-mcp-app/*
!apps/morning-mcp-app/src
apps/webapp/e2e
specs
.github
.claude
**/playwright-report
**/test-results
**/blob-report
**/.last-run.json
**/.DS_Store

# Secrets / per-clone files
# Any per-env / local config (config.dev/prod/test.json, config.player_prod.json, *-preview.json, ...):
# only the safe placeholder template and the schema ship in an image. Env config is mounted at runtime.
**/config/config.*.json
!**/config/config.example.json
!**/config/config.schema.json
apps/webapp/backend/auth/*.hash
apps/webapp/backend/logs
**/test_logs
**/*.log.*
apps/webapp/backend/auth/password.hash
creds
docker/docker-compose.*.local.yml
